Subject: [PATCH] build: pin UN1CA vendor load policy and reproducible CPIO

The four retained target firmware vendor partitions request the same two
modules. Derive their dependency closure from the freshly verified build,
not a previous ROM/kernel cache. Keep image assembly in the upstream script.
The caller normalizes ramdisk mtimes before this reproducible CPIO operation.

diff --git a/build/unica/vendor.modules.load b/build/unica/vendor.modules.load
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/unica/vendor.modules.load
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+input_booster_lkm.ko
+sec_debug_sched_info.ko
diff --git a/build/scripts/images.sh b/build/scripts/images.sh
--- a/build/scripts/images.sh
+++ b/build/scripts/images.sh
@@ -65,6 +65,6 @@ build_images() {
 
     echo -e "\n$(log_info "Building vendor_boot image...")"
     cd "$RAMDISK_DIR"
-    find . | cpio --quiet -o -H newc -R root:root | gzip -9 > "../ramdisk.cpio.gz"
+    find . -print0 | LC_ALL=C sort -z | cpio --null --reproducible --quiet -o -H newc -R root:root | gzip -n -9 > "../ramdisk.cpio.gz"
     cd ..
 
